      "sample_resolution_status": "multi_resolved",
      "parameters": {},
      "result_summary": "Confirmed monosubstitution pattern of PSBPhBr, high degree of functionalization of quinolate polymers, tetracoordinated boron centers, and functionalization degree of copolymer PSBPhQ-H-co-PSSiMe<sub>3</sub>.",
      "derived_property_ids": [
        "prop_s5_001"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "block_id": "P_1_19",
          "page": 1,
          "bbox": [
            81.0,
            594.0,
            483.0,
            959.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "Transfer of a single phenyl group to the boron moieties was evident from multinuclear NMR spectroscopy and further confirmed by comparison of the polymer data withthoseofthecorrespondingmolecularcompound(<sup>t</sup>BuPh)<sub>2</sub>BBr."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "P_1_22",
          "page": 1,
          "bbox": [
            511.0,
            803.0,
            915.0,
            958.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "The organoboron quinolate polymers were fully characterized by <sup>1</sup>H, $^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C } ,$and $^ { 1 1 } \\mathrm { B }$NMR spectroscopy."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "P_2_32",
          "page": 2,
          "bbox": [
            511.0,
            493.0,
            915.0,
            729.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "In contrast, when we monitored the <sup>1</sup>H NMR spectra of the tert-butylphenyl-substituted quinolate polymers both in wet and oxygenated solvents and as solids in air, no sign of decomposition was found for at least 4 weeks, and the GPC traces were virtually identical to those of the freshly prepared polymer samples."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "P_4_51",
          "page": 4,
          "bbox": [
            81.0,
            371.0,
            483.0,
            789.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "The degree of functionalization for the isolated copolymer PSBPhQ-H-co-PSSiMe was calculated to be 10.5% according to <sup>1</sup>H NMR integration and 12.8% according to GPC-MALLS, which is very close to the feed ratio of BBr<sub>3</sub> to $\\mathrm { S i M e } _ { 3 }$functional groups."
        }
      ],
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
    },
    {
      "characterization_id": "char002",
      "method_raw": "gel permeation chromatography (GPC)",
      "method_normalized": "GPC",
      "sample_ids": [
        "s001",
